# 03 – SAP PP Customizing and Organizational Configuration

## 1. Configuration Overview

As part of the PHOS Smart Lamp manufacturing project, SAP organizational and planning parameters were defined to support the integration of purchasing, inventory management, and production planning processes.

The configuration was designed around the manufacturing requirements established during the preliminary engineering analysis.

The main areas addressed were:

- Purchasing organization and material classification.
- Material Requirements Planning (MRP) responsibilities.
- Production scheduling responsibilities.
- Storage location organization.
- Material planning parameters.

## 2. Purchasing Configuration

A purchasing group and material groups were defined to support procurement activities and material classification.

| Configuration Element | SAP Code | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Purchasing Group | ZPS | Purchasing Department |
| Material Group | ZPMC | Chemical Materials |
| Material Group | ZPME | Electronic Materials |
| Material Group | ZPMM | Metallic Materials |
| Material Group | ZPMP | Polymeric Materials |

The material groups were established to classify purchased materials according to their characteristics and role in the manufacturing process.

## 3. Production Planning Responsibilities

Planning responsibilities were defined to support the management of material requirements and manufacturing schedules.

| Configuration Element | SAP Code | Assigned Function |
|---|---|---|
| MRP Controller | ZPP | Material Requirements Planning |
| Production Scheduler | ZPC | Production Scheduling |

The MRP Controller was designated as the responsible planning entity for monitoring material requirements and procurement proposals.

The Production Scheduler was designated to coordinate manufacturing scheduling activities.

## 4. Storage Location Configuration

Three storage locations were defined to distinguish materials according to their position in the manufacturing process.

| SAP Code | Storage Location | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| ZPMP | Raw Materials | Storage of purchased materials and components |
| ZPSL | Semi-Finished Products | Storage of internally manufactured intermediate products |
| ZPPF | Finished Products | Storage of completed PHOS lamps |

This structure supports inventory visibility and the separation of materials throughout the production process.

## 5. Material Master Planning Parameters

The project adopted differentiated planning parameters according to the material type.

| Material Type | MRP Type | Lot-Sizing Procedure |
|---|---|---|
| ROH – Raw Materials | VB | FX |
| HALB – Semi-Finished Products | PD | EX |
| FERT – Finished Products | PD | EX |

These settings were selected to align procurement and production planning with the manufacturing model developed in Excel.

Raw materials followed manual reorder point planning with fixed procurement quantities.

Semi-finished and finished products followed deterministic material requirements planning with lot-for-lot sizing.

The detailed planning rationale and lot-sizing calculations are documented in **02 – MRP Planning Strategies**.

## 6. Integration with the PHOS Manufacturing Process

The organizational configuration supports the relationship between purchasing, production planning, and inventory management.

The intended operational structure is:

1. Raw materials are classified into the corresponding material groups.
2. Procurement activities are organized through the purchasing group.
3. Material requirements are managed through the designated MRP responsibility.
4. Manufacturing scheduling is coordinated through the production scheduling responsibility.
5. Purchased materials, intermediate products, and finished lamps are managed through their respective storage locations.

This configuration provides an organizational foundation for the PHOS manufacturing process in SAP S/4HANA.

## 7. Conclusion

The SAP configuration phase focused on defining the organizational elements and planning responsibilities required for the PHOS manufacturing scenario.

The purchasing group, material groups, MRP controller, production scheduler, and storage locations were structured to support material procurement, production planning, and inventory management.

Together with the MRP parameters documented in the previous section, these settings establish the organizational framework for the PHOS Smart Lamp manufacturing process.
